{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "d/dx x^3 - 3x = 3x^2 - 3\n  holds for every real x\n  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 2e-15)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "diff", "ucas": "diff x^3 - 3x", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "diff", "vars": ["x"], "order": 1, "derivative": "3x^2 - 3"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "central_differences", "points": 201, "max_diff": 2.277073149684367e-15, "passed": true}], "files": [], "text": "d/dx x^3 - 3x = 3x^2 - 3\n  holds for every real x\n  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 2e-15)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "∂²/∂y∂x x^4 + x^2*y + y^3 = 2x\n  holds wherever the formula is defined\n  check: each order matches central differences at 200 points (max relative difference 3e-13)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "diff", "ucas": "diff x^4 + x^2*y + y^3 x y", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "diff", "vars": ["x", "y"], "order": 2, "derivative": "2x"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "central_differences", "points": 200, "max_diff": 3.156728346193397e-13, "passed": true}], "files": [], "text": "∂²/∂y∂x x^4 + x^2*y + y^3 = 2x\n  holds wherever the formula is defined\n  check: each order matches central differences at 200 points (max relative difference 3e-13)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "∇ x^2*y*z = (2x*y*z, x^2*z, x^2*y)\n  ∂/∂x x^2*y*z = 2x*y*z\n  ∂/∂y x^2*y*z = x^2*z\n  ∂/∂z x^2*y*z = x^2*y\n  holds wherever the formulas are defined\n  check: every entry matches central differences at 300 points (max relative difference 4e-13)\n  at (x = 1, y = 2, z = 3): (12, 3, 2), |∇| = 12.52996409\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "grad", "ucas": "grad x^2*y*z at 1, 2, 3", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "grad", "gradient": [{"var": "x", "derivative": "2x*y*z"}, {"var": "y", "derivative": "x^2*z"}, {"var": "z", "derivative": "x^2*y"}], "at_value": [12, 3, 2], "at_norm": 12.529964086141668}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "central_differences", "points": 300, "max_diff": 4.426777143884743e-13, "passed": true}], "files": [], "text": "∇ x^2*y*z = (2x*y*z, x^2*z, x^2*y)\n  ∂/∂x x^2*y*z = 2x*y*z\n  ∂/∂y x^2*y*z = x^2*z\n  ∂/∂z x^2*y*z = x^2*y\n  holds wherever the formulas are defined\n  check: every entry matches central differences at 300 points (max relative difference 4e-13)\n  at (x = 1, y = 2, z = 3): (12, 3, 2), |∇| = 12.52996409\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "∇² x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 6\n  ∂²/∂x² x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 2\n  ∂²/∂y² x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 2\n  ∂²/∂z² x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 2\n  holds wherever the formulas are defined\n  check: every entry matches central differences at 600 points (max relative difference 4e-13)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "laplacian", "ucas": "laplacian x^2 + y^2 + z^2", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "laplacian", "laplacian": "6", "harmonic": false}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "central_differences", "points": 600, "max_diff": 4.065799189564532e-13, "passed": true}], "files": [], "text": "∇² x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 6\n  ∂²/∂x² x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 2\n  ∂²/∂y² x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 2\n  ∂²/∂z² x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 2\n  holds wherever the formulas are defined\n  check: every entry matches central differences at 600 points (max relative difference 4e-13)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Hessian of x^2*y + y^2 (row i, column j: ∂²/∂j∂i):\n  [ 2y   2x ]   ∂/∂x\n  [ 2x   2  ]   ∂/∂y\n  det = 4y - 4x^2\n  holds wherever the formulas are defined\n  check: every entry matches central differences at 400 points (max relative difference 3e-13)\n  symmetric (the mixed partials agree) at 100 of 100 sample pairs\n  at (x = 1, y = 2):\n  [ 4          2          ]\n  [ 2          2          ]\n  det = 4\n  the gradient is not 0 there (largest component 5): not a critical point\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 5, "ok": true, "cmd": "hessian", "ucas": "hessian x^2*y + y^2 at 1, 2", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "hessian", "matrix": [["2y", "2x"], ["2x", "2"]], "det": "4y - 4x^2", "at_classification": "not a critical point", "at_det": 4}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "central_differences", "points": 400, "max_diff": 3.337025213289339e-13, "passed": true}], "files": [], "text": "Hessian of x^2*y + y^2 (row i, column j: ∂²/∂j∂i):\n  [ 2y   2x ]   ∂/∂x\n  [ 2x   2  ]   ∂/∂y\n  det = 4y - 4x^2\n  holds wherever the formulas are defined\n  check: every entry matches central differences at 400 points (max relative difference 3e-13)\n  symmetric (the mixed partials agree) at 100 of 100 sample pairs\n  at (x = 1, y = 2):\n  [ 4          2          ]\n  [ 2          2          ]\n  det = 4\n  the gradient is not 0 there (largest component 5): not a critical point\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 6, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Jacobian of (x^2 + y, x*y) wrt (x, y): row i = the gradient of function i\n  [ 2x   1 ]\n  [ y    x ]\n  det = 2x^2 - y\n  holds wherever the formulas are defined\n  check: every entry matches central differences at 400 points (max relative difference 3e-13)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 6, "ok": true, "cmd": "jacobian", "ucas": "jacobian x^2+y, x*y wrt x, y", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "jacobian", "wrt": ["x", "y"], "matrix": [["2x", "1"], ["y", "x"]], "det": "2x^2 - y"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "central_differences", "points": 400, "max_diff": 3.2836671187648304e-13, "passed": true}], "files": [], "text": "Jacobian of (x^2 + y, x*y) wrt (x, y): row i = the gradient of function i\n  [ 2x   1 ]\n  [ y    x ]\n  det = 2x^2 - y\n  holds wherever the formulas are defined\n  check: every entry matches central differences at 400 points (max relative difference 3e-13)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 7, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Wronskian matrix of exp(x), exp(2x) (row k: the k-th derivatives wrt x)\n  [ exp(x)   exp(2x)  ]   the functions\n  [ exp(x)   2exp(2x) ]   d/dx\n  W = det = exp(3x)\n  (W equals the numeric determinant at all 200 sample points of [-10, 10])\n  check: every entry matches central differences at 402 points (max relative difference 3e-14)\n  linearly independent: W(-1/20) = 0.8607079764 != 0, so the functions are independent on every interval containing x = -1/20\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 7, "ok": true, "cmd": "wronskian", "ucas": "wronskian exp(x), exp(2x)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "wronskian", "var": "x", "matrix": [["exp(x)", "exp(2x)"], ["exp(x)", "2exp(2x)"]], "wronskian": "exp(3x)", "independent": true, "witness_x": -0.05000000000000071, "witness_w": 0.8607079764250559}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "central_differences", "points": 402, "max_diff": 3.182400464154972e-14, "passed": true}], "proof": {"kind": "numeric", "text": "W != 0 at a sample point"}, "files": [], "text": "Wronskian matrix of exp(x), exp(2x) (row k: the k-th derivatives wrt x)\n  [ exp(x)   exp(2x)  ]   the functions\n  [ exp(x)   2exp(2x) ]   d/dx\n  W = det = exp(3x)\n  (W equals the numeric determinant at all 200 sample points of [-10, 10])\n  check: every entry matches central differences at 402 points (max relative difference 3e-14)\n  linearly independent: W(-1/20) = 0.8607079764 != 0, so the functions are independent on every interval containing x = -1/20\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 8, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "limit of sin(x)/x as x -> 0:\n  0/0: L'Hôpital: lim (cos(x))/(1) = lim cos(x)\n  = 1 (from both sides)\n  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.9983341665, 0.9999934896, 0.9999999746, 0.9999999999, 1, 1\n    extrapolated (Richardson): 1 (estimated error 0): agrees\n  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.9983341665, 0.9999934896, 0.9999999746, 0.9999999999, 1, 1\n    extrapolated (Richardson): 1 (estimated error 0): agrees\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 8, "ok": true, "cmd": "limit", "ucas": "limit sin(x)/x as x -> 0", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "limit", "var": "x", "at": "0", "side": "both", "limit": {"kind": "number", "value": 1, "text": "1"}}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "numeric_left", "points": 22, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true, "text": "Richardson-extrapolated values approaching the point"}, {"kind": "numeric_right", "points": 22, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true, "text": "Richardson-extrapolated values approaching the point"}], "files": [], "text": "limit of sin(x)/x as x -> 0:\n  0/0: L'Hôpital: lim (cos(x))/(1) = lim cos(x)\n  = 1 (from both sides)\n  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.9983341665, 0.9999934896, 0.9999999746, 0.9999999999, 1, 1\n    extrapolated (Richardson): 1 (estimated error 0): agrees\n  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.9983341665, 0.9999934896, 0.9999999746, 0.9999999999, 1, 1\n    extrapolated (Richardson): 1 (estimated error 0): agrees\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 9, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "limit of 1/x as x -> 0+ (from the right):\n  1/x -> inf (the numerator -> 1, x -> 0+)\n  = inf\n  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 10, 160, 2560, 40960, 655360, 20971520\n    the values grow without bound (+): agrees\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 9, "ok": true, "cmd": "limit", "ucas": "limit 1/x as x -> 0+", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "limit", "var": "x", "at": "0", "side": "+", "limit": {"kind": "+inf", "text": "inf"}}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "limit of 1/x as x -> 0+ (from the right):\n  1/x -> inf (the numerator -> 1, x -> 0+)\n  = inf\n  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 10, 160, 2560, 40960, 655360, 20971520\n    the values grow without bound (+): agrees\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 10, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "limit of 1/x as x -> 0- (from the left):\n  1/x -> -inf (the numerator -> 1, x -> 0-)\n  = -inf\n  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): -10, -160, -2560, -40960, -655360, -20971520\n    the values grow without bound (-): agrees\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 10, "ok": true, "cmd": "limit", "ucas": "limit 1/x as x -> 0-", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "limit", "var": "x", "at": "0", "side": "-", "limit": {"kind": "-inf", "text": "-inf"}}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "limit of 1/x as x -> 0- (from the left):\n  1/x -> -inf (the numerator -> 1, x -> 0-)\n  = -inf\n  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): -10, -160, -2560, -40960, -655360, -20971520\n    the values grow without bound (-): agrees\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 11, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "limit of sin(1/x) as x -> 0:\n  1/x -> inf (the numerator -> 1, x -> 0+)\n  1/x -> inf: sin(1/x) keeps oscillating between -1 and 1\n  = none (it oscillates between -1 and 1)\n  the limit does not exist\n  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.5440211109, -0.2194252584, -0.3875871276, 0.08491512332, 0.9779231634, -0.4379663196\n    the values do not settle (the last ones lie in [-0.993585, 0.977923]): consistent\n  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): -0.5440211109, 0.2194252584, 0.3875871276, -0.08491512332, -0.9779231634, 0.4379663196\n    the values do not settle (the last ones lie in [-0.977923, 0.993585]): consistent\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 11, "ok": true, "cmd": "limit", "ucas": "limit sin(1/x) as x -> 0", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "limit", "var": "x", "at": "0", "side": "both", "limit": {"kind": "oscillates", "text": "none (it oscillates between -1 and 1)"}}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "limit of sin(1/x) as x -> 0:\n  1/x -> inf (the numerator -> 1, x -> 0+)\n  1/x -> inf: sin(1/x) keeps oscillating between -1 and 1\n  = none (it oscillates between -1 and 1)\n  the limit does not exist\n  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.5440211109, -0.2194252584, -0.3875871276, 0.08491512332, 0.9779231634, -0.4379663196\n    the values do not settle (the last ones lie in [-0.993585, 0.977923]): consistent\n  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): -0.5440211109, 0.2194252584, 0.3875871276, -0.08491512332, -0.9779231634, 0.4379663196\n    the values do not settle (the last ones lie in [-0.977923, 0.993585]): consistent\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 12, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Maclaurin (Taylor at 0) series of sin(x) at x = 0, through order 7:\n  sin(x) = x - x^3/6 + x^5/120 - x^7/5040 + O(x^8)\n  as x -> 0; coefficients c_k = f^(k)(0)/k!: 0 1 0 -1/6 0 1/120 0 -1/5040\n  check: the coefficients agree with Taylor-jet arithmetic (long double) to 0\n  check: |f - P| = 2.76e-15 at x = 0 ± 1/10, 5.38e-18 at ± 1/20, 1.02e-20 at ± 1/40 (at rounding level)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 12, "ok": true, "cmd": "taylor", "ucas": "taylor sin(x) x at 0 order 7", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "taylor", "var": "x", "at": 0, "order": 7, "polynomial": "x - x^3/6 + x^5/120 - x^7/5040", "coefficients": ["0", "1", "0", "-1/6", "0", "1/120", "0", "-1/5040"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "taylor_jet", "points": 8, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true, "text": "coefficients against long double Taylor-jet arithmetic"}], "files": [], "text": "Maclaurin (Taylor at 0) series of sin(x) at x = 0, through order 7:\n  sin(x) = x - x^3/6 + x^5/120 - x^7/5040 + O(x^8)\n  as x -> 0; coefficients c_k = f^(k)(0)/k!: 0 1 0 -1/6 0 1/120 0 -1/5040\n  check: the coefficients agree with Taylor-jet arithmetic (long double) to 0\n  check: |f - P| = 2.76e-15 at x = 0 ± 1/10, 5.38e-18 at ± 1/20, 1.02e-20 at ± 1/40 (at rounding level)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 13, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Taylor series of log(x) at x = 1, through order 4:\n  log(x) = x - 1 - (x - 1)^2/2 + (x - 1)^3/3 - (x - 1)^4/4 + O((x - 1)^5)\n  as x -> 1; coefficients c_k = f^(k)(1)/k!: 0 1 -1/2 1/3 -1/4\n  check: the coefficients agree with Taylor-jet arithmetic (long double) to 0\n  check: |f - P| = 2.18e-06 at x = 1 ± 1/10, 6.52e-08 at ± 1/20, 1.99e-09 at ± 1/40 (shrinks like h^5.0; expected >= 5)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 13, "ok": true, "cmd": "taylor", "ucas": "taylor log(x) x at 1 order 4", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "taylor", "var": "x", "at": 1, "order": 4, "polynomial": "x - 1 - (x - 1)^2/2 + (x - 1)^3/3 - (x - 1)^4/4", "coefficients": ["0", "1", "-1/2", "1/3", "-1/4"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "taylor_jet", "points": 5, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true, "text": "coefficients against long double Taylor-jet arithmetic"}], "files": [], "text": "Taylor series of log(x) at x = 1, through order 4:\n  log(x) = x - 1 - (x - 1)^2/2 + (x - 1)^3/3 - (x - 1)^4/4 + O((x - 1)^5)\n  as x -> 1; coefficients c_k = f^(k)(1)/k!: 0 1 -1/2 1/3 -1/4\n  check: the coefficients agree with Taylor-jet arithmetic (long double) to 0\n  check: |f - P| = 2.18e-06 at x = 1 ± 1/10, 6.52e-08 at ± 1/20, 1.99e-09 at ± 1/40 (shrinks like h^5.0; expected >= 5)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 14, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "on the curve x^2 + y^2 - 1 = 0, y as a function of x:\n  dy/dx = -F_x/F_y = -x/y\n  holds where F_y = 2y != 0 (the implicit function theorem: there y is locally a differentiable function of x)\n  check: matches the slope of the curve (points solved by bisection and Newton) at 12 points (max relative difference 2e-12)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 14, "ok": true, "cmd": "implicit", "ucas": "implicit x^2+y^2=1 for y wrt x", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "implicit", "var": "x", "function": "y", "derivative": "-x/y", "headline": "on the curve x^2 + y^2 - 1 = 0, y as a function of x:", "details": ["dy/dx = -F_x/F_y = -x/y", "holds where F_y = 2y != 0 (the implicit function theorem: there y is locally a differentiable function of x)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "matches the slope of the curve (points solved by bisection and Newton) at 12 points (max relative difference 2e-12)"}], "files": [], "text": "on the curve x^2 + y^2 - 1 = 0, y as a function of x:\n  dy/dx = -F_x/F_y = -x/y\n  holds where F_y = 2y != 0 (the implicit function theorem: there y is locally a differentiable function of x)\n  check: matches the slope of the curve (points solved by bisection and Newton) at 12 points (max relative difference 2e-12)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 15, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "∫ x^2 dx\n  = x^3/3 + C\n  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [0, 1] (max difference 1.1e-16)\n  from 0 to 1: F(1) - F(0) = 0.333333333333333\n  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 15 evaluations): 0.333333333333333, estimated error 3.7e-15\n  the two agree to 0\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 15, "ok": true, "cmd": "integrate", "ucas": "integrate x^2 wrt x from 0 to 1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "integrate", "var": "x", "integrand": "x^2", "antiderivative": "x^3/3", "definite": {"from": 0, "to": 1, "symbolic": 0.3333333333333333, "numeric": 0.3333333333333333, "error_estimate": 3.6666666666666666e-15, "evaluations": 15, "value": 0.3333333333333333}}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "derivative", "points": 401, "max_diff": 1.1102230246251565e-16, "passed": true, "text": "d/dx of the antiderivative against the integrand"}, {"kind": "numeric_integral", "points": 15, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true, "text": "F(b) - F(a) against adaptive Gauss-Kronrod"}], "files": [], "text": "∫ x^2 dx\n  = x^3/3 + C\n  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [0, 1] (max difference 1.1e-16)\n  from 0 to 1: F(1) - F(0) = 0.333333333333333\n  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 15 evaluations): 0.333333333333333, estimated error 3.7e-15\n  the two agree to 0\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 16, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "∫ 1/x^2 dx\n  = -1/x + C\n  method: partial fractions, Hermite reduction for the repeated factors\n  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 400 points of [-1, 1] (max difference 0)\n  numeric: the integrand is undefined or infinite inside the interval (singular or divergent)\n  quasi-Monte Carlo does not settle either: 8 replicates of 4096 Sobol points give 3.81e+04 with a standard error of 6.3e+03: no value (a pole, or an integral that does not exist)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 16, "ok": true, "cmd": "integrate", "ucas": "integrate 1/x^2 wrt x from -1 to 1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "integrate", "var": "x", "integrand": "1/x^2", "antiderivative": "-1/x", "method": "partial fractions, Hermite reduction for the repeated factors", "definite": {"from": -1, "to": 1, "value": null}, "qmc": {"dimensions": 1, "points": 4096, "replicates": 8, "seed": 1, "scrambling": "digital shift", "infinite_box": false, "estimate": 38067.277687871094, "converged": false, "value": null}}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "derivative", "points": 400, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true, "text": "d/dx of the antiderivative against the integrand"}], "files": [], "text": "∫ 1/x^2 dx\n  = -1/x + C\n  method: partial fractions, Hermite reduction for the repeated factors\n  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 400 points of [-1, 1] (max difference 0)\n  numeric: the integrand is undefined or infinite inside the interval (singular or divergent)\n  quasi-Monte Carlo does not settle either: 8 replicates of 4096 Sobol points give 3.81e+04 with a standard error of 6.3e+03: no value (a pole, or an integral that does not exist)\n"}, "isError": false}}
